s://github.com/jeasmith","id":6818323,"login":"jeasmith","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTgzMjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/commits/4d736d069f862aa8812f58ab4ba38d557a3eb47d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:08:30Z","email":"jeasmith@me.com","name":"Jamie Smith"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T14:08:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: sketch the article library schema and redraw the first build (#106)\n\n* docs: sketch the article library schema\n\nDerives the library''s tables from CONTEXT.md and the pipeline and route\ncontracts, and flags the four constraints the sketch cannot settle: where an\nexempt newsletter''s category comes from, whether a verdict is one per article,\nwhether a brief is immutable in the database, and where the export lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: exempt newsletters take their source''s category\n\nSettles the first open constraint in the schema sketch. Newsletters bypass\ntriage and the write contract returns no category, so code assigns the\nsource''s category on the exemption path rather than giving the column a\nsecond writer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: one verdict per article; promotion sits outside it\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: briefs are immutable because they are transient\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: fingerprint source text instead of retaining it\n\nRevises ADR-0017 the same day it merged. The database holds relations; a\nsource is identified by its URL. A hash, length and retrieval time on each\nwriting attempt keep what retention was for, and remove the one table that\ngrew without bound.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: redraw the first build to the original problem\n\nGitHub is the private write surface, so the app has no sign-in, private\npages or private role. Defers the backlog UI, roundup expansion into\ntriage, per-run coverage pages, the gated migration job and the restore\nrehearsal. Export is a monthly compressed pg_dump to a private repository.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: address review on the schema sketch\n\nPipeline role reads its own tables; migrate role gets journal and backfill\nDML; the newsletter exemption is the directly arrived article only; one brief\nper article is a unique constraint; the dump repository rotates twelve files\non a single commit instead of accumulating history.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: address the second review on the schema sketch\n\nTriage predicate carries the roundup deferral; the issue row has no draft\nstate and exists only if the date published; diagnostics are redacted at\nwrite time and the dump omits source endpoints pending #94; the ~200 figures\nin the contracts are labelled pre-redraw.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a2e2031c5c9cc66c60f7a43bff9ea50a8f69898","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/git/trees/6a2e2031c5c9cc66c60f7a43bff9ea50a8f69898"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/git/commits/4d736d069f862aa8812f58ab4ba38d557a3eb47d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a2e2031c5c9cc66c60f7a43bff9ea50a8f69898\nparent 624412706972385f190c14760dea35fd0000172b\nauthor Jamie Smith <jeasmith@me.com> 1788703710 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788703710 +0100\n\ndocs: sketch the article library schema and redraw the first build (#106)\n\n* docs: sketch the article library schema\n\nDerives the library''s tables from CONTEXT.md and the pipeline and route\ncontracts, and flags the four constraints the sketch cannot settle: where an\nexempt newsletter''s category comes from, whether a verdict is one per article,\nwhether a brief is immutable in the database, and where the export lands.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: exempt newsletters take their source''s category\n\nSettles the first open constraint in the schema sketch. Newsletters bypass\ntriage and the write contract returns no category, so code assigns the\nsource''s category on the exemption path rather than giving the column a\nsecond writer.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: one verdict per article; promotion sits outside it\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: briefs are immutable because they are transient\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: fingerprint source text instead of retaining it\n\nRevises ADR-0017 the same day it merged. The database holds relations; a\nsource is identified by its URL. A hash, length and retrieval time on each\nwriting attempt keep what retention was for, and remove the one table that\ngrew without bound.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: redraw the first build to the original problem\n\nGitHub is the private write surface, so the app has no sign-in, private\npages or private role. Defers the backlog UI, roundup expansion into\ntriage, per-run coverage pages, the gated migration job and the restore\nrehearsal. Export is a monthly compressed pg_dump to a private repository.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: address review on the schema sketch\n\nPipeline role reads its own tables; migrate role gets journal and backfill\nDML; the newsletter exemption is the directly arrived article only; one brief\nper article is a unique constraint; the dump repository rotates twelve files\non a single commit instead of accumulating history.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* docs: address the second review on the schema sketch\n\nTriage predicate carries the roundup deferral; the issue row has no draft\nstate and exists only if the date published; diagnostics are redacted at\nwrite time and the dump omits source endpoints pending #94; the ~200 figures\nin the contracts are labelled pre-redraw.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnXPeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhiMQAH9lwiSza6Uarq6kTt4K/4fW\ni1E9b2Ha2pc8OYPxXKOoGx4by7SsA32d1Gf+8tcKkLhTN5ndE6RIUBw+dEm2H0V/\n2CwMtafxLMVZAhwrQfOX/0lhXa2z0mCNybDWwk0AYLcnUOFpXfDx5dXCftMjXBEX\n3Ed+tS7/Z5iMJj3S+yaLpzi+EgBwcJ5aKVqUOPyoqApiKGY79/pIKv9M9q6iPFfq\nrSy7HgeIPnxSgc0CHR3fjeFj4pnyAerOBUZkMuIDMR/1+lVv33BEuvT3GrNNrpKQ\ng8nTuk0DJ/mlL21IIly9PpgEzuCeFCLf03CrkiA4Wtez/hUbhRi/ZcpDAACu0CEj\nWsHpLVwYMOuqe2J0J6jdv+ev/6xD4BFrTV9H5hnUf8FIVveBKk/GhpwVM6b1Wd/O\nx2VXZAWUd2BmCjnwno1IILTcSAncU2WPqDauB+QGo4d+CvrbDSqP0WntEXOuAIER\n5C735uF1rzvuZHNJEqzKxRe6ldPjh+o1h46LfULICg/va+SDxkefHEuohyMR1qz7\nEKXrrEhdUs1Zy7YqWWuMHCBAlBWwzZFbra3KXkvc/RZYapD+71yRjp8zeexpyG4f\nU7/gznekEqO51cuMpYOaV2nzu6upGi5pmLiycQAKEPBdlWOR4KS/mfbt52WtrMVK\nYzpm95AqjCXwgqh+M1ET\n=asn9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T14:08:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://githu