hNzcwNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/jeasmith/ithilien/commit/735db425fdba8fb0d779f23f098f1b5703782810","sha":"735db425fdba8fb0d779f23f098f1b5703782810","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/commits/735db425fdba8fb0d779f23f098f1b5703782810"}],"sha":"8e29f35e24be4fa383aacb4142ae362c44a77072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/commits/8e29f35e24be4fa383aacb4142ae362c44a77072"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6818323?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jeasmith","id":6818323,"login":"jeasmith","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4MTgzMjM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeasmith","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/commits/735db425fdba8fb0d779f23f098f1b5703782810/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:10Z","email":"jeasmith@me.com","name":"Jamie Smith"},"comment_count":1,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T09:58:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Split Ithilien into a Turborepo microfrontends monorepo (#80)\n\n* Split into a Turborepo monorepo with Vercel microfrontends\n\nRadar, an architectural digest, needs its own deployment lifecycle without\nmoving off the shared origin. Vercel Microfrontends routes paths to separate\nprojects at the edge, so Ithilien keeps / while Radar takes /radar, and each\ndeploys independently.\n\nThe single-app layout could not express that, so the repository becomes a pnpm\nworkspace driven by Turborepo. Turborepo also starts Vercel''s local proxy\nalongside the dev servers, which is what makes local routing behave like\nproduction. Shared design tokens move to packages/ui so the two apps cannot\ndrift apart visually.\n\nRouting is asserted in CI against the real microfrontends.json, so a path\nclaimed by the wrong application fails the build rather than silently sending\ntraffic to the wrong deployment.\n\nOpen port 3024 for local development, not 3000 — that is the proxy.\n\nSee docs/adr/0015-turborepo-monorepo.md and\ndocs/adr/0016-vercel-microfrontends.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address review feedback on the microfrontends split\n\nKeep the app favicon out of Git LFS. The .gitattributes exception is\npath-specific, so moving the file into apps/ithilien silently re-enrolled it\nand committed a 130-byte pointer. Next.js reads this ICO during the build and\nVercel does not smudge LFS, which is what failed the preview deployment.\n\nGive the production servers distinct ports. Root `pnpm start` fans out to both\napplications and bare `next start` defaults to 3000, so the second app died on\nan address already in use.\n\nDeclare @vitest/coverage-v8. Both apps select `provider: \"v8\"` but neither\ndepended on it, so `pnpm test:coverage` failed on a missing dependency.\n\nDrop the shadcn `hooks` alias, which pointed at a subpath that packages/ui does\nnot export, and correct the docs: pnpm-workspace.yaml already globs apps/*, the\nLSP entry needs --silent, and two directory-tree fences lacked a language.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"cec5d9fed9b6457dc0ad63eb5380221733b15672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/git/trees/cec5d9fed9b6457dc0ad63eb5380221733b15672"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jeasmith/ithilien/git/commits/735db425fdba8fb0d779f23f098f1b5703782810","verification":{"payload":"tree cec5d9fed9b6457dc0ad63eb5380221733b15672\nparent 78251d22892d27c317111e888522cd7e652b4666\nauthor Jamie Smith <jeasmith@me.com> 1788170290 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788170290 +0000\n\nSplit Ithilien into a Turborepo microfrontends monorepo (#80)\n\n* Split into a Turborepo monorepo with Vercel microfrontends\n\nRadar, an architectural digest, needs its own deployment lifecycle without\nmoving off the shared origin. Vercel Microfrontends routes paths to separate\nprojects at the edge, so Ithilien keeps / while Radar takes /radar, and each\ndeploys independently.\n\nThe single-app layout could not express that, so the repository becomes a pnpm\nworkspace driven by Turborepo. Turborepo also starts Vercel''s local proxy\nalongside the dev servers, which is what makes local routing behave like\nproduction. Shared design tokens move to packages/ui so the two apps cannot\ndrift apart visually.\n\nRouting is asserted in CI against the real microfrontends.json, so a path\nclaimed by the wrong application fails the build rather than silently sending\ntraffic to the wrong deployment.\n\nOpen port 3024 for local development, not 3000 — that is the proxy.\n\nSee docs/adr/0015-turborepo-monorepo.md and\ndocs/adr/0016-vercel-microfrontends.md.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Address review feedback on the microfrontends split\n\nKeep the app favicon out of Git LFS. The .gitattributes exception is\npath-specific, so moving the file into apps/ithilien silently re-enrolled it\nand committed a 130-byte pointer. Next.js reads this ICO during the build and\nVercel does not smudge LFS, which is what failed the preview deployment.\n\nGive the production servers distinct ports. Root `pnpm start` fans out to both\napplications and bare `next start` defaults to 3000, so the second app died on\nan address already in use.\n\nDeclare @vitest/coverage-v8. Both apps select `provider: \"v8\"` but neither\ndepended on it, so `pnpm test:coverage` failed on a missing dependency.\n\nDrop the shadcn `hooks` alias, which pointed at a subpath that packages/ui does\nnot export, and correct the docs: pnpm-workspace.yaml already globs apps/*, the\nLSP entry needs --silent, and two directory-tree fences lacked a language.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlVAyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJS4QAF78S7XJfQXhbKCA3Sse/LdZ\nIiuhj1DKBWgsbAR3F+YQH7+Ca7hsJQ3m7tlqB+OY6ObOqTZitI9qaleWiYeh6HZ0\nAx+ekVdPsDjpV6YkyDhO9gtZwtYQ8lH8kDXO2VhZzdrKvt9VEaDT5Kreb7OmY893\nMWBGlTciVy6k1tneQuciV62s07JS9Vw+/VURjyemuOq6/AednZiHKV1ez/aWKGly\n24Cu6a5LtVEOHSLAj31B3ts6ARzeNVkL7r1BLRXwDPu5tShtwmmiFs3Nl5YgrWKF\nZ/7WhzdyQX+CsuPlswCbaTu8apilzKd27kowZ57mc7RS1sJ4lrhpf+zqMJ+JLURl\n4cyakMtZjP3ejZ0KgpKoNK1PZAZ2TX7Z3ywIh+JLFrRRX6lHSjS6jx1b526HIhkz\nW1mCYO10snvJOn9MYFCIIooWJOVTnf8ogg0OdkmFlZSUS33lER/kEI2OAiS66s+d\nO+kFGveSWDhDcoFO23YgjDrzi9rQWFN2s5aIto2Djudw7iu/4B+hvfdG0MOIWjSX\njhO3mZDlvQuuxf/DOpFZiu1etc5/4jgig5gZydwCm88kqZwiyjVsnb+N9SSFE3Vy\no3Zm/I4BAvOCTWiNzaVItzk8OkRdmzlV5ybK4U5qXZ1mJDw26hjLp06AsA4UxL09\nqI8P+LVCxh1AYEyZhSIy\n=sxjo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T09:58:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.c