"2026-08-26T21:06:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"E2E: Widen the Keycloak readiness window and simplify the profile teardown (#211)\n\n* E2E: Widen the Keycloak readiness window for cold starts\n\nThe readiness probe allowed roughly 150s before Docker gives up: a 30s\nstart period plus twelve 10s retries. A cold Keycloak boot that imports\nthe e2e realm measured ~90s on a developer machine, and the management\nport stays closed until the import finishes, so a slower CI runner can\noverrun the window. When it expires, server-core and server-intro-course\nnever start, because both gate on service_healthy, and the whole run\nfails before a single spec executes. The suite has not yet run on a\nGitHub runner, so widen the window before it does.\n\nAlso trim the probe comment to the two facts that are not visible in the\ncommand itself, and drop the claim that a TCP connect would race the\nrealm import: the management port is not opened until startup completes.\n\n* E2E: Restore the edited developer profile from the constants\n\nSnapshotting the profile in beforeAll guards against a UDID the seed does\nnot have: every seeded profile has all three UDID columns NULL, and\nputDeveloperProfile already defaults them to null, so the snapshot\nrestores exactly what the constants restore.\n\nIt also introduces a way to lose the fixture for good. Retries run in a\nfresh worker, so beforeAll re-snapshots. If a restore ever fails, the\nretry captures the edited Apple ID and pins it as the new baseline, and\nthe table spec that asserts the seeded value has nothing to fall back on.\nRestoring from the constants converges on the seed no matter how the test\nended, and it keeps this teardown consistent with the rest of the suite,\nwhich asserts and restores against constants throughout.\n\nIf the seed grows UDIDs later, they belong in the constants next to the\nApple ID and the GitLab username, like every other seeded field.","tree":{"sha":"909699c9060df778ec369ae8b7f866d620c7c3f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/trees/909699c9060df778ec369ae8b7f866d620c7c3f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/commits/40be1cd062158b46e668d8021cda646c5bc0655c","verification":{"payload":"tree 909699c9060df778ec369ae8b7f866d620c7c3f4\nparent 9e570ff0962f7dbab4a9285036ba7eb76c659d49\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1787778406 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787778406 +0200\n\nE2E: Widen the Keycloak readiness window and simplify the profile teardown (#211)\n\n* E2E: Widen the Keycloak readiness window for cold starts\n\nThe readiness probe allowed roughly 150s before Docker gives up: a 30s\nstart period plus twelve 10s retries. A cold Keycloak boot that imports\nthe e2e realm measured ~90s on a developer machine, and the management\nport stays closed until the import finishes, so a slower CI runner can\noverrun the window. When it expires, server-core and server-intro-course\nnever start, because both gate on service_healthy, and the whole run\nfails before a single spec executes. The suite has not yet run on a\nGitHub runner, so widen the window before it does.\n\nAlso trim the probe comment to the two facts that are not visible in the\ncommand itself, and drop the claim that a TCP connect would race the\nrealm import: the management port is not opened until startup completes.\n\n* E2E: Restore the edited developer profile from the constants\n\nSnapshotting the profile in beforeAll guards against a UDID the seed does\nnot have: every seeded profile has all three UDID columns NULL, and\nputDeveloperProfile already defaults them to null, so the snapshot\nrestores exactly what the constants restore.\n\nIt also introduces a way to lose the fixture for good. Retries run in a\nfresh worker, so beforeAll re-snapshots. If a restore ever fails, the\nretry captures the edited Apple ID and pins it as the new baseline, and\nthe table spec that asserts the seeded value has nothing to fall back on.\nRestoring from the constants converges on the seed no matter how the test\nended, and it keeps this teardown consistent with the rest of the suite,\nwhich asserts and restores against constants throughout.\n\nIf the seed grows UDIDs later, they belong in the constants next to the\nApple ID and the GitLab username, like every other seeded field.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj1VmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHacQAFvyKbg/leY4+c/dIn/GATBd\nbPuU8Bo5iSyZe6Ob8JF7Gu4vViax6KpK4EY2Oqz7mF635PJr89a9Dr1uCNh0E1Ws\nXUc7Ah9WzZQQKL+pTRdYzPjzZLhGu2fTu8KpmamaaLi33xZ/Ky0y2KAg2GhB53Dd\nYPDnBInsvhODM8GMtNXhqMIiIOSKCbrb3NedQJJCUsKG5R2i5uoqwkqIqujUpo1C\nY++xV1vgWAunBjzx9V45jT0XDvlkh5UdYYveDkRilucOtbeMHJ0XkdyfUXmGBCBb\nOmRFGor3ZmnIDdOger1bGnLsYpg7L7eWhB/4DOBG0xCOcSZIiUkM5aQ/hxvYzr1c\nsqX1imqtI88K7UxGIMUs3OrS4OvOelthKBluLTVXoM63VTqm2rpL0De8gmZjKqgB\nK1Q15qEMoT1/IE1VBpcCfTIqH6gZwOKPq/qc4nAJVNmF5V1WsWNeTBssiuqdbo5h\nhuOwt1FO8ThZsMXFhTSbLTqYVqYwZBESYTi6KDgY692zAcafJuzu5S74xeY6NpQS\ng9pBDWF6DtAHD1Mo79pR9ZKb+WIhtds6jhjCPhRRYE+aUZsXNUVPn+uV8wbTui3F\nQLNkUkhGnYxSlGRbgNp7dOx4yjkMFyvrTugxHTezDwJsh0HaxEe3UXWH5LUfRjJv\n3CeVCH51vcVZnDQmyaGY\n=nTb2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T21:06:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web