rs/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commits/a3468b3b64d59edd726f4ff9a9c53ca54fae3e10/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T20:48:40Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T20:48:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace deprecated Sentry SendDefaultPII with DataCollection (#212)\n\nsentry-go v0.48.0 deprecated ClientOptions.SendDefaultPII, so staticcheck''s\nSA1019 fails the lint-server job on main and on every open branch.","tree":{"sha":"71b4c70a7ca1781592286b02ec18fcf7362fc87f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/trees/71b4c70a7ca1781592286b02ec18fcf7362fc87f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/commits/a3468b3b64d59edd726f4ff9a9c53ca54fae3e10","verification":{"payload":"tree 71b4c70a7ca1781592286b02ec18fcf7362fc87f\nparent 28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1787777320 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787777320 +0200\n\nReplace deprecated Sentry SendDefaultPII with DataCollection (#212)\n\nsentry-go v0.48.0 deprecated ClientOptions.SendDefaultPII, so staticcheck''s\nSA1019 fails the lint-server job on main and on every open branch.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj1EoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwFUQAFiq7phepa2sf99cmfoDcMmx\nei4ngarmhEaa0qFLvjLqZc4F+MB5jUoTwZcRiXDMYVBIwJRos9Iq/RNKAbMVqmA+\nFQMZQ6750v6ZY9sRthlwoNjLOVwcS/kB/9kKA4+fyvZ4VKUIor0NHv2O7ry3xbx/\nXwP8Ihs4lJtjQrBVkVrBENJ0eiOHMrViyvL8Ma63h5ZRJBtn57EDev+LAmlzc9tO\nATBFi0OjOJNhDU8gKzGE7Df2PywGB3yJls6iLNvYp8UnX8dcVBu+sLEVFK8WBS6t\naICekcDv7JDhUb6HH6Am6s3Cqa0FD6larjINNMDSiWDCLE3hw4k5rK5N1Ly/e12A\n0URIi8P5Ut/HAY1Be2xyX6oskNpXG/sK9T0NuXXdy6No00BxOXYhUGyek23LGwOx\nrJLJ0AXhOjkVDS2DyazZ6t+/GDST8Jviy9PHbvcQZl+ILN9AI14y/cm+ES1UcENx\nyNRQI++nsQuhdAFlNBQxO8Fljmhe5toWTF9CcHru5yR3FbNRix6ylmzG3r89KUBz\nnd8pykf4t0jzBQXMCeKJ9Y2KfIoBV9GL67/06wKo4LXHXrdXG5xyHlW9CLvK03x3\nDprgOydrfVofcfKd0/XPTHlaEiTAR38Yn9wWMhyyuFnxgVz+XXwEkjQFNgSB+Mg2\nW5RXeH2zSBMGKCZTY+Z5\n=gNYP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T20:48:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commit/a3468b3b64d59edd726f4ff9a9c53ca54fae3e10","node_id":"C_kwDORg3GrNoAKGEzNDY4YjNiNjRkNTllZGQ3MjZmNGZmOWE5YzUzY2E1NGZhZTNlMTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commit/28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec","sha":"28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commits/28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec"}],"sha":"a3468b3b64d59edd726f4ff9a9c53ca54fae3e10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commits/a3468b3b64d59edd726f4ff9a9c53ca54fae3e10"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53191688?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/rappm","id":53191688,"login":"rappm","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTkxNjg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rappm","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/commits/28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:04:01Z","email":"53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Maximilian Rapp"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T21:04:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add E2E testing to the intro course (#205)\n\n* Server: Expose the standard service info endpoint\n\nRegister promptTypes.RegisterInfoEndpoint on the intro-course/api group, the\nsame contract every other PROMPT phase service already publishes. The health\nflag is a live DB ping.\n\nThis gives the intro course two things it was missing: an entry on core''s\nsystem status page, and an unauthenticated readiness probe. The E2E stack uses\nit as its readiness gate — the server image is distroless, so it has no\ncontainer healthcheck, and asserting the /info JSON (rather than a bare status)\nalso proves the reverse-proxy wiring, since an SPA fallback would answer 200\nwith HTML for a misrouted path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Client: Make the tutor table search box actually filter\n\nThe search input held state and rendered a magnifier, but the query was never\napplied to the rows — typing anything left the table unchanged. Filter on name,\nemail, matriculation number, university login, and GitLab username, and drive\nthe existing \"No tutors found.\" empty state off the filtered list.\n\nFound by the new E2E suite, which asserted the documented behaviour and failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Client: Add test ids to elements with no stable selector\n\nPage navigation and most primary actions are already reachable by role and\ntext, so this only covers what is not:\n\n- seat cells, whose visible text is initials or a position number, leaving the\n  seat name addressable only through a title attribute\n- peer group cards, group rows, and members\n- the seat and peer assignment status badges\n- developer profile and tutor table rows, plus the inline GitLab username input\n- the four Yes/No pairs on the developer profile survey and the three Help\n  dialog triggers, all of which repeat the same label on one page\n\nYesNoButtons gains a required `name` prop for that last case. No behaviour\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove the screenshot harness, superseded by the E2E stack\n\nThe harness could not catch a regression in the real app and could not be run\nfrom a clean checkout:\n\n- `playwright` was neither in client/package.json nor in yarn.lock, and no npm\n  script invoked screenshot.cjs\n- ScreenshotApp.tsx re-implemented the pages in a MemoryRouter, bypassing\n  routes/index.tsx, IntroCourseDataShell, the zustand store, and the app''s axios\n  instance — around 37 KB of parallel code to keep in sync\n- it had already drifted from the API contract, calling /developer-profile/all\n  where the app and server use /developer_profile\n- cmd/devserver re-implemented most handlers rather than reusing the real\n  routers, and mocked core at /api/v2 paths core does not serve\n- screenshotStubs/ was dead code with no importers\n\nserver/database_dumps/e2e_seed.sql is kept and now feeds the E2E stack\ndirectly. The variadic authMiddlewareOverride parameters stay too — the Go\nrouter tests exercise them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add the Docker Compose stack, seeds, and realm\n\nStands the real PROMPT core shell up around this repository''s server and\nmicro-frontend, with a real Keycloak and real databases. Core is pulled prebuilt\nfrom ghcr.io rather than built, which works because of three properties of the\npublished core client:\n\n1. it is a production build, so its Module Federation remote for this repo is\n   baked in as the relative URL /intro-course-developer/remoteEntry.js\n2. this repo''s remote already sets publicPath ''auto'' and exposes the routes,\n   sidebar, and provide entry points core expects\n3. INTRO_COURSE_HOST is already in core''s env.template.js; left empty, the\n   component''s axios baseURL falls back to the browser origin\n\ne2e/nginx/client-core.conf stands in for prod Traefik: /intro-course/api/ keeps\nits prefix, /intro-course-developer/ has it stripped, and /api/ reaches core —\nthat last one because the tutor page calls one core endpoint through the\nintro-course axios instance, whose baseURL is the browser origin.\n\nSeeds are split so they can be maintained independently. seed/core/10_core_seed.sql\nis a verbatim copy of the platform repo''s dump, refreshable with a file copy;\n20_intro_course.sql adds the phase type (fixed UUID, since core''s startup init\nmatches by name and would otherwise mint a random one), the phase, a graph edge,\nand 56 background students. The intro-course database mounts the migrations\nthemselves plus the existing fixture, so server/db/migration stays the single\nsource of truth, with a pin file so the server''s boot-time migrate is a no-op.\n\nThe realm is the platform repo''s e2e realm plus this repo''s host ports and the\n/Prompt/ios2425-iPraktikumFull group tree — core creates that tree when a course\nis created through the UI, and the seeded course never went through it.\n\nHost ports are offset from the platform repo''s e2e stack so both can run at once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add the Playwright harness\n\nThe runner is itself a Compose service, so a local run and a CI run are\nidentical and the browser can address every service by Docker name — Chromium\nhard-codes localhost to loopback and ignores /etc/hosts, so an in-container\nbrowser cannot reach the stack any other way.\n\nglobal-setup gates on four things before any spec runs: core''s /api/hello, the\ncore client, the intro-course /info JSON through the proxy, and the remote''s\nremoteEntry.js being JavaScript rather than an SPA fallback. Each failure names\nthe URL it gave up on, which turns a misconfigured proxy from an opaque\nLoadingError in every browser spec into one clear message. It then drives the\nreal Keycloak login form once per role and saves a storageState.\n\nThe suite runs with workers: 1. Every spec shares the single seeded course phase,\nunlike the platform repo which can afford a fixture phase per spec file.\n\nsrc/db.ts is deliberate and deliberately small: POST /developer_profile is a\ncreate rather than an upsert and has no DELETE counterpart, so only a real row\ndelete lets the survey spec survive a retry.\n\nThe runner image typechecks the suite at build time, since Playwright transpiles\nwithout checking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add specs covering every intro-course page\n\n148 tests over the seven routes, in two Playwright projects:\n\n- mf-smoke: the remote and its sidebar render inside the core shell for a\n  lecturer and a student. One assertion covers the whole Module Federation path,\n  since a failed remote makes core render a LoadingError instead\n- seat assignment: the seeded 89-seat Rechnerhalle plan, the four workflow\n  steps, table/grid and tutor/peer-group/seat view modes, seat swapping,\n  Smart Assign, and Reset Assignments\n- peer assignments: the seeded 17 groups, Generate, Clear All, and an\n  Edit -> Save round trip\n- developer profiles: sorting, filtering, and the per-row edit dialog\n- tutor import: the Keycloak group gate, the tutor table, inline GitLab\n  username editing, and the import dialog\n- participants and mailing\n- student journey: survey submission as the student without a profile, and the\n  seat/tutor/peer display as the one with\n- permissions: all seven routes times all six roles. course-editor is the\n  interesting negative — it clears core''s course gate but not the routes''\n  requiredPermissions\n- api: the info endpoint, unauthenticated rejection, the role matrix on every\n  endpoint, student-scoped reads, and phase scoping\n\nMutating specs snapshot their slice of the fixture and replay it in afterEach,\nso each test can run alone and a retry starts clean. GitLab-dependent actions\nassert the surfaced error rather than reaching for a real GitLab: the stack has\nno token on purpose.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Wire the suite into CI and document it\n\ntest-e2e.yml builds the stack, runs the containerized runner, tears down, and\nuploads both the HTML report and test-results (traces, videos, and the\nglobal-setup diagnostic screenshots) on failure. dev.yml gates it on lint and vet\nso an obvious mistake fails in seconds, and runs it in parallel with the server\ntests; deployment does not depend on it.\n\nNo Node setup or browser install step is needed — everything lives in Compose,\nso CI runs exactly what `make test-e2e` runs locally. The three core images are\npublic on ghcr.io, so no registry login is required.\n\ne2e/README.md covers the stack layout, the seeded users and data, readiness, the\ntwo deviations from the upstream realm copy, and the conventions for adding\ntests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Address review feedback on the E2E stack\n\nGate the Keycloak service on /health/ready rather than a bare TCP accept on\nthe management port, so the servers cannot begin OIDC discovery against a\nrealm the import has not created yet. The image ships neither curl nor wget,\nso the request is spoken over bash''s /dev/tcp; bash is named explicitly\nrather than relying on /bin/sh being a link to it.\n\nMove the two fixture restores into hooks that run on failure: the tutor\nGitLab username was restored inside the test body, and the developer profile\nwas rebuilt from constants rather than from a snapshot, which would erase any\nUDID the seed grows later.\n\nAlso preserve the Playwright exit status in test-e2e-ui, drop checkout\ncredential persistence in CI, and bound the /intro-course/api/info database\nping with a timeout so the public endpoint cannot park a request goroutine on\nan exhausted pool.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f0b1e014d6984541765d76a1d0359c0c8af9616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/trees/8f0b1e014d6984541765d76a1d0359c0c8af9616"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prompt-edu/prompt-intro-course/git/commits/28215d2228fc21a69661a826b3ad6661fc9deeec","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f0b1e014d6984541765d76a1d0359c0c8af9616\nparent 693819ae086d45c45e1d7b416fc2d78f57bf8d35\nauthor Maximilian Rapp <53191688+rappm@users.noreply.github.com> 1787432641 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787432641 +0200\n\nAdd E2E testing to the intro course (#205)\n\n* Server: Expose the standard service info endpoint\n\nRegister promptTypes.RegisterInfoEndpoint on the intro-course/api group, the\nsame contract every other PROMPT phase service already publishes. The health\nflag is a live DB ping.\n\nThis gives the intro course two things it was missing: an entry on core''s\nsystem status page, and an unauthenticated readiness probe. The E2E stack uses\nit as its readiness gate — the server image is distroless, so it has no\ncontainer healthcheck, and asserting the /info JSON (rather than a bare status)\nalso proves the reverse-proxy wiring, since an SPA fallback would answer 200\nwith HTML for a misrouted path.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Client: Make the tutor table search box actually filter\n\nThe search input held state and rendered a magnifier, but the query was never\napplied to the rows — typing anything left the table unchanged. Filter on name,\nemail, matriculation number, university login, and GitLab username, and drive\nthe existing \"No tutors found.\" empty state off the filtered list.\n\nFound by the new E2E suite, which asserted the documented behaviour and failed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Client: Add test ids to elements with no stable selector\n\nPage navigation and most primary actions are already reachable by role and\ntext, so this only covers what is not:\n\n- seat cells, whose visible text is initials or a position number, leaving the\n  seat name addressable only through a title attribute\n- peer group cards, group rows, and members\n- the seat and peer assignment status badges\n- developer profile and tutor table rows, plus the inline GitLab username input\n- the four Yes/No pairs on the developer profile survey and the three Help\n  dialog triggers, all of which repeat the same label on one page\n\nYesNoButtons gains a required `name` prop for that last case. No behaviour\nchanges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove the screenshot harness, superseded by the E2E stack\n\nThe harness could not catch a regression in the real app and could not be run\nfrom a clean checkout:\n\n- `playwright` was neither in client/package.json nor in yarn.lock, and no npm\n  script invoked screenshot.cjs\n- ScreenshotApp.tsx re-implemented the pages in a MemoryRouter, bypassing\n  routes/index.tsx, IntroCourseDataShell, the zustand store, and the app''s axios\n  instance — around 37 KB of parallel code to keep in sync\n- it had already drifted from the API contract, calling /developer-profile/all\n  where the app and server use /developer_profile\n- cmd/devserver re-implemented most handlers rather than reusing the real\n  routers, and mocked core at /api/v2 paths core does not serve\n- screenshotStubs/ was dead code with no importers\n\nserver/database_dumps/e2e_seed.sql is kept and now feeds the E2E stack\ndirectly. The variadic authMiddlewareOverride parameters stay too — the Go\nrouter tests exercise them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add the Docker Compose stack, seeds, and realm\n\nStands the real PROMPT core shell up around this repository''s server and\nmicro-frontend, with a real Keycloak and real databases. Core is pulled prebuilt\nfrom ghcr.io rather than built, which works because of three properties of the\npublished core client:\n\n1. it is a production build, so its Module Federation remote for this repo is\n   baked in as the relative URL /intro-course-developer/remoteEntry.js\n2. this repo''s remote already sets publicPath ''auto'' and exposes the routes,\n   sidebar, and provide entry points core expects\n3. INTRO_COURSE_HOST is already in core''s env.template.js; left empty, the\n   component''s axios baseURL falls back to the browser origin\n\ne2e/nginx/client-core.conf stands in for prod Traefik: /intro-course/api/ keeps\nits prefix, /intro-course-developer/ has it stripped, and /api/ reaches core —\nthat last one because the tutor page calls one core endpoint through the\nintro-course axios instance, whose baseURL is the browser origin.\n\nSeeds are split so they can be maintained independently. seed/core/10_core_seed.sql\nis a verbatim copy of the platform repo''s dump, refreshable with a file copy;\n20_intro_course.sql adds the phase type (fixed UUID, since core''s startup init\nmatches by name and would otherwise mint a random one), the phase, a graph edge,\nand 56 background students. The intro-course database mounts the migrations\nthemselves plus the existing fixture, so server/db/migration stays the single\nsource of truth, with a pin file so the server''s boot-time migrate is a no-op.\n\nThe realm is the platform repo''s e2e realm plus this repo''s host ports and the\n/Prompt/ios2425-iPraktikumFull group tree — core creates that tree when a course\nis created through the UI, and the seeded course never went through it.\n\nHost ports are offset from the platform repo''s e2e stack so both can run at once.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add the Playwright harness\n\nThe runner is itself a Compose service, so a local run and a CI run are\nidentical and the browser can address every service by Docker name — Chromium\nhard-codes localhost to loopback and ignores /etc/hosts, so an in-container\nbrowser cannot reach the stack any other way.\n\nglobal-setup gates on four things before any spec runs: core''s /api/hello, the\ncore client, the intro-course /info JSON through the proxy, and the remote''s\nremoteEntry.js being JavaScript rather than an SPA fallback. Each failure names\nthe URL it gave up on, which turns a misconfigured proxy from an opaque\nLoadingError in every browser spec into one clear message. It then drives the\nreal Keycloak login form once per role and saves a storageState.\n\nThe suite runs with workers: 1. Every spec shares the single seeded course phase,\nunlike the platform repo which can afford a fixture phase per spec file.\n\nsrc/db.ts is deliberate and deliberately small: POST /developer_profile is a\ncreate rather than an upsert and has no DELETE counterpart, so only a real row\ndelete lets the survey spec survive a retry.\n\nThe runner image typechecks the suite at build time, since Playwright transpiles\nwithout checking.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Add specs covering every intro-course page\n\n148 tests over the seven routes, in two Playwright projects:\n\n- mf-smoke: the remote and its sidebar render inside the core shell for a\n  lecturer and a student. One assertion covers the whole Module Federation path,\n  since a failed remote makes core render a LoadingError instead\n- seat assignment: the seeded 89-seat Rechnerhalle plan, the four workflow\n  steps, table/grid and tutor/peer-group/seat view modes, seat swapping,\n  Smart Assign, and Reset Assignments\n- peer assignments: the seeded 17 groups, Generate, Clear All, and an\n  Edit -> Save round trip\n- developer profiles: sorting, filtering, and the per-row edit dialog\n- tutor import: the Keycloak group gate, the tutor table, inline GitLab\n  username editing, and the import dialog\n- participants and mailing\n- student journey: survey submission as the student without a profile, and the\n  seat/tutor/peer display as the one with\n- permissions: all seven routes times all six roles. course-editor is the\n  interesting negative — it clears core''s course gate but not the routes''\n  requiredPermissions\n- api: the info endpoint, unauthenticated rejection, the role matrix on every\n  endpoint, student-scoped reads, and phase scoping\n\nMutating specs snapshot their slice of the fixture and replay it in afterEach,\nso each test can run alone and a retry starts clean. GitLab-dependent actions\nassert the surfaced error rather than reaching for a real GitLab: the stack has\nno token on purpose.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Wire the suite into CI and document it\n\ntest-e2e.yml builds the stack, runs the containerized runner, tears down, and\nuploads both the HTML report and test-results (traces, videos, and the\nglobal-setup diagnostic screenshots) on failure. dev.yml gates it on lint and vet\nso an obvious mistake fails in seconds, and runs it in parallel with the server\ntests; deployment does not depend on it.\n\nNo Node setup or browser install step is needed — everything lives in Compose,\nso CI runs exactly what `make test-e2e` runs locally. The three core images are\npublic on ghcr.io, so no registry login is required.\n\ne2e/README.md covers the stack layout, the seeded users and data, readiness, the\ntwo deviations from the upstream realm copy, and the conventions for adding\ntests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* E2E: Address review feedback on the E2E stack\n\nGate the Keycloak service on /health/ready rather than a bare TCP accept on\nthe management port, so the servers cannot begin OIDC discovery against a\nrealm the import has not created yet. The image ships neither curl nor wget,\nso the request is spoken over bash''s /dev/tcp; bash is named explicitly\nrather than relying on /bin/sh being a link to it.\n\nMove the two fixture restores into hooks that run on failure: the tutor\nGitLab username was restored inside the test body, and the developer profile\nwas rebuilt from constants rather than from a snapshot, which would erase any\nUDID the seed grows later.\n\nAlso preserve the Playwright exit status in test-e2e-ui, drop checkout\ncredential persistence in CI, and bound the /intro-course/api/info database\nping with a timeout so the public endpoint cannot park a request goroutine on\nan exhausted pool.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqig7BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhmoQAIYKwzjMpsVcvFqF5T6vGzHF\neL3t8gzVHxeHenJZ6R60ff/+tmjrIM6hBsbbY6QItWxfSYUPQ3mtEpgP5WDrjb+h\n7QGxbe4B+gsFi+SQ0bWC6b0S3imQn0E5qSLdORJOtUAFhLf6MsqhRulOqnH2/w9d\nl8IWaSmtqTqhNLZhw37vH8r3w3TZChMibm9D2weManacvNoaGPJKMSaPxISzDvno\niDy4/cpF7D1LwvJhy1IQWUgqDEzxjrsSgzM92WYLaxhtfCUrTPmX8jyJLg4gMYBF\nGnj4Rd2ggq4zBdLu8Cd2CVKEq8hCyGmDWsL2sPxCQ3xxCvEboyhibrwldrHzPeAM\nBQPkyhw/aSzaqcH+W/B2nmwqpGq/P/ge2mdFn/Coq9Yc+ZUdBmBJejTaVsnuMYsq\nlczYN+VuteqovIwjhlvaZUqCuXy/kca2beyoFfB4Blm6sc2379cJCz6EODZAcqY1\nKhunAm/kLruX3CmaYFzQGzMPCgZ9psCGD1PhRpyzlKdAD0/Z/F7Faj56Ic1vCdH0\nCEXGCQk6KlYmAsJooaPOI+MzrF9LemizdJYLCXXhKjJlTntGj3AO+HGCAv2WnVE5\nIE0FAoBbXp5MW84b3lQVK35TW89sgTYmccL0gYJhwXX2/o07l5KDKljBttN0LwVl\n6XNcj1InpbZO+ojOBLo7\n=IMWc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T21:04:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":