ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joebarbere","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joebarbere/claude-hello-world/commits/18c8c8d30db025f86635b403183ab110e4b1cc47/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-15T03:08:40Z","email":"joe.barbere@gmail.com","name":"Joe Barbere"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-15T03:08:40Z","email":"joe.barbere@gmail.com","name":"Joe Barbere"},"message":"Fix Podman dirs, purge images, add Traefik tests\n\nEnsure Podman-based local cluster builds are reliable and add e2e checks for Traefik. Create required hostPath directories inside the Podman VM before starting pods to avoid kube-up failures; add a .containerignore to shrink container build contexts and avoid OOMs; and force-remove known base images in CI before builds to work around corrupted local image stores. Also add Traefik health e2e tests to verify dashboard API and routing.\n\nChanged/added files:\n- Added .containerignore\n- Modified apps/shell/project.json (kube-up now creates /var/log/traefik and /var/log/nginx)\n- Added tests in apps/shell-e2e/src/eks.spec.ts (Traefik dashboard + router/access-log checks)\n- Updated CI workflows (.github/workflows/eks-e2e.yml, eks-e2e-full.yml) to remove potential corrupted base images\n- Updated SUMMARY.md with notes about the fix","tree":{"sha":"6823f01d5e453a4c923be2560b4956cb0b0f3682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joebarbere/claude-hello-world/git/trees/6823f01d5e453a4c923be2560b4956cb0b0f3682"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/joebarbere/claude-hello-world/git/commits/18c8c8d30db025f86635b403183ab110e4b1cc47","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/198229?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joebarbere/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joebarbere/followers","following_url":"https://ap